@hidden
Feature: Steps that do not rot (hidden examples)

  Background:
    Given a GDD project in a git repository with the protected paths:
      """
      [protected]
      all = ["gdd/**", "bin/**"]
      builder_build = ["features/**", "tests/steps/**"]
      builder_test = ["src/**"]
      """
    And the zone map:
      """
      default = "yellow"

      [[zone]]
      color = "red"
      paths = ["src/storage/**"]
      reason = "Losing the user's drafts"
      """
    And the models:
      """
      [orchestrator]
      integration = "claude"
      model = "opus"

      [builder.yellow]
      integration = "claude"
      model = "sonnet"

      [builder.red]
      integration = "claude"
      model = "opus"

      [builder_test]
      integration = "claude"
      model = "sonnet"

      [reviewer]
      integration = "codex"
      model = "gpt-6"

      [families]
      "opus" = "anthropic"
      "sonnet" = "anthropic"
      "gpt" = "openai"
      """

  Scenario: Every agent gets the same rule for steps
    When I run "gdd agents install"
    Then it succeeds
    And the file ".agents/skills/gdd-build-test/SKILL.md" contains "reuse a step that already says the same"
    And the file ".agents/skills/gdd-review/SKILL.md" contains "a new step that says what an existing step already says"
